# DCAPT — Cline rules

- `reference/scoring-spec.md` is the only source of truth for the priority formula. Any scoring
  code (the DB trigger, the client preview) must match it exactly; if you change the formula,
  update the spec first.
- Reference data — climate risks/strategies/interventions, departments/schemes, co-benefit
  items, funding-source tiers, scoring weights — lives in Supabase tables. Never hardcode it in
  app code.
- `priority_score` is always computed server-side by `compute_priority_score()` in
  `supabase/migrations/00002_scoring.sql`. Never write it from the client.
- RLS policies are the real access boundary, not the app. Never bypass RLS with a service-role
  key from client code.
- `schemes_master.csv` is provisional — most scheme names are placeholders pending real
  government policy notes. Don't treat it as finished data.
- Don't port code or patterns from the `legacy-streamlit-snapshot` git tag. It's a superseded
  prototype with two known bugs and a formula that's since been reworked.
